{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/milind-soni/OpenMausBot/pulls/3074","id":4913223588,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT1lw988AAAABJNnXpA","html_url":"https://github.com/milind-soni/OpenMausBot/pull/3074","diff_url":"https://github.com/milind-soni/OpenMausBot/pull/3074.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/milind-soni/OpenMausBot/pull/3074.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/milind-soni/OpenMausBot/issues/3074","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/milind-soni/OpenMausBot/pulls/3074/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/milind-soni/OpenMausBot/pulls/3074/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/milind-soni/OpenMausBot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/milind-soni/OpenMausBot/issues/3074/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/milind-soni/OpenMausBot/statuses/f1d25d56582fe28d0db16a5088aee2967e7aa84d","number":3074,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Run when my AI limit resets, and continue on the backup engine","user":{"login":"milind-soni","id":46266943,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjY2OTQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46266943?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni","html_url":"https://github.com/milind-soni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What the person gets\n\n- **A new automation \"when\": the AI limit resets.** \"When your Claude limit resets, Scout finishes the report.\" Once (default) or every reset. From chat (\"run this when my limit resets\" → `create_trigger when=limit_reset`), from the editor's When (\"When my AI limit resets\" + engine picker + once / every time), and from the calendar.\n- **The stopped turn's button.** A turn stopped by a usage limit with a known reset shows **\"Continue at 3:40 PM when your limit resets\"**. One click creates a one-time limit-reset automation in that conversation (the usual card with Pause, Edit, Undo). It runs in that same conversation and is told the previous turn hit the limit.\n- **The bot does it itself.** TRIGGER_PROMPT and the tool description cover it; a turn on an engine at ≥ 90 % has that on its clock line (\"Claude's usage limit is 92% used; it resets …\"), so the bot can set up its continuation and say so (no approval card, like every trigger).\n- **Near-limit warning.** \"Claude: 92% used · resets 3:40 PM\" on the Automations page with **Move to after reset** for schedules due before the reset whose bot uses that engine (only their next run moves), plus a compact notice in that bot's chat header.\n- **Calendar.** Each engine's next known reset is a labelled marker (\"Claude resets 3:40 PM\"). Dropping a bot from the sidebar on it opens the quick composer for a limit-reset automation; dropping an automation on it switches it to run at that reset.\n- **Backup engine.** With Automatic recovery on and a backup configured (bot fallback list or workspace backup), a usage-limit refusal continues on the backup with one line: \"Claude hit its limit (resets 3:40 PM), so Codex took over.\" After the reset, the next turn in that conversation goes back, with one line. No allowed backup → the Continue button. **Never** moves to another sign-in of the same subscription engine (that circumvents provider usage limits); another engine or a pay-per-use key is fine.\n\n## How the reset time is derived\n\nSchedule: `{ type: \"limit_reset\", engine, repeat: \"once\" | \"every_reset\", at }`. `at` is derived on the server (reset + 60 s), never taken from input; `null` while unknown.\n\n`server/limit-resets.ts` keeps one limit per engine instance:\n- **Plan usage** (`plan-usage.ts`): Claude `five_hour` / `seven_day` (`utilization`, `resets_at`); Codex `primary_window` / `secondary_window` (`used_percent`, `reset_at`, assigned by window length).\n- **Refusals:** Claude's `rate_limit_info.resetsAt` (`runtime.error.limitResetsAt`); Codex now also sets `limitResetsAt` from its words \"try again at 5:23 PM\" / \"…at Oct 17th, 2026 5:23 PM\" (host local time).\n- Rule: windows at ≥ 100 % decide and the latest of their resets counts; otherwise the fullest window. A live refusal wins unless usage shows a later window still full; it is kept 10 min past its time. Unknown → \"runs when the limit resets (time not known yet)\" and usage is polled every 5 min while an automation waits. Every usage refresh or refusal retimes the waiting automations. `every_reset` never runs twice for one reset.\n- Usage is read at most every 5 minutes for the warnings. Sealed test fixtures no longer read this machine's keychain for plan usage.\n\n## Failover\n\n- Claude's startup hold, which already proves a signed-out refusal, also proves a usage-limit refusal (synthetic `usage_limit_reached` + error result with no new cost, process stopped) → `TurnUsageLimitRefusedError` → `startTurn`'s existing backup path.\n- An engine the clock knows is refusing raises the same error before dispatch, so Codex/Grok turns and automation runs also go to the backup without spending a refused turn. A Codex automation run refused with a known reset is restarted at once for the backup instead of waiting for the reset.\n- `limit-failovers.json` remembers `{thread → from, to, resetsAt}` for the switch back.\n\n## Moved out (pinned files shrink)\n\n`routine-schedules.ts` (from routines.ts), `routine-request-schemas.ts` (from routine-requests.ts), `routine-run-card.ts` (from index.ts), `projectCalls` → `lib/routine-calendar.ts`, ChatView's lucide import on one line. Pins lowered: index.ts 17285→17259, routines.ts 1804→1651, routine-requests.ts 1677→1484, ChatView.tsx 1492→1482, RoutineCalendarPage.tsx 1763→1750. store.tsx, App.tsx, electron/main.mjs unchanged. Catalog goldens re-pinned (create_trigger `when` + `engine` + `repeat`; budgets within 2 %).\n\n## Tests\n\n- `server/limit-resets.test.ts`: derivation from Claude and Codex fixtures, blocked vs fullest, refusal precedence, expiry, unknown time, Codex words, near-limit line.\n- `server/routines-limit-reset.test.ts`: derived time, recompute when the reset moves, once vs every reset, unknown time, late wake still runs, restart, Move to after reset, backup restart of a refused run.\n- `server/limit-reset-requests.test.ts`: create_trigger `when=limit_reset`, the card and Undo, default engine, duplicates, resume, and the routes (Continue creates the automation in the same thread, idempotent; after-reset; limits list).\n- `server/drivers/claude-auth-recovery.test.ts`: the usage-limit refusal hold.\n- `server/limit-failover.test.ts`: same-engine sign-ins refused, API key allowed, switch back after reset, unknown reset waits an hour.\n- `server/limit-reset.e2e.test.ts` (real server, fake Claude/Codex, a test clock hook that shortens the post-reset minute): button → automation → reset → run continues the same conversation; failover to Codex with the line, pre-dispatch skip, switch back after reset; a same-engine backup is never used and the button is offered.\n- `src/components/limit-resets.test.ts`: warning + Move to after reset, chat notice, Continue button, calendar marker and drops onto it, sentences.\n- Mutation-checked: 36 unit-level and 7 end-to-end mutations, each caught.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added visibility into AI engine usage limits, including near-limit warnings and expected reset times.\n  * Added automations that run once or repeatedly after an engine’s usage limit resets. Create and manage them from the calendar, or move routines to run after a reset.\n  * Added an option to continue a chat after its limit resets, plus automatic recovery using an eligible backup engine.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved handling of usage-limit refusals so unfinished turns can be resumed and recovery respects reset timing.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-18T22:04:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T23:22:28Z","closed_at":"2026-10-18T23:22:28Z","merged_at":"2026-10-18T23:22:28Z","merge_commit_sha":"53d9803aea32c11104a5301805089a5d6b40cf8c","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"milind-soni:feat/run-when-limit-resets","ref":"feat/run-when-limit-resets","repo":{"id":1331261687,"node_id":"R_kgDOT1lw9w","name":"OpenMausBot","full_name":"milind-soni/OpenMausBot","owner":{"login":"milind-soni","id":46266943,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjY2OTQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46266943?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni","html_url":"https://github.com/milind-soni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/milind-soni/re